                                         Highlights
                                         Impact of (a)synchronism on ECA: towards a new classification1
                                         Isabel Donoso-Leiva, Eric Goles, Martı́n Rı́os-Wilson, Sylvain Sené
arXiv:2505.10645v1 [cs.DM] 15 May 2025




                                                • A new formal approach to analyze the impact on elementary cellular
                                                  automata (ECA) of asynchronism/synchronism is presented.

                                                • Concepts of asyncronism/synchronism are considered through funda-
                                                  mental families of periodic update modes.

                                                • A new classification of ECA based on computational complexity is of-
                                                  fered, measured through the length of their longest reached limit cycle
                                                  is proposed.

                                                • Numerical experiments are analyzed for specific and well known chaotic
                                                  and complex ECA, namely 54, 90, 110 and 150, through measures of
                                                  density and energy.


